# Consent Flow: {{ rubric_name }}

## Context

- slug: mcp-security
- owner: <role:person>
- approver: <role:person>
- produced_at: <YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ>
- scope: `<scope>` (local_desktop / remote_single_tenant / remote_multi_tenant)
- client: <host name and version from the inventory>
- consent policy: `<consent_policy>` (per_call / per_session / always_allow_listed_only)

## Shared rules (apply to every primitive)

- Rule r1: the consent surface is visually distinct from model output and from tool text; the user cannot mistake it for chat.
- Rule r1: a decision is cached at most for the session; a new session asks again.
- Rule r4: a server calling a method it did not declare in `initialize` gets no prompt at all; the call is rejected and logged.
- Rule r5: consent granted to one server never carries over to another server, even for a same-named tool.
- Rule r6: every prompt shown and every decision taken is written to the audit log with server_id, tool_name, caller_session, arguments_hash, outcome, timestamp.
- Rule r7: the prompt names the server by its verified identity (signed manifest / pinned cert); an unverified server is blocked before any prompt.

## Tools (actions)

- trigger: first call to `<server>__<tool>` in this session
- surface: {{ surface }}
- shows: verified server name, tool name, the server-supplied description labelled "text from server", the argument summary
- rule r3: the description and the arguments are displayed as quoted data, never interpreted
- options: allow once | allow for session | deny
- cache scope: <per_call: never; per_session: until session end; always_allow_listed_only: only for tools on the allow-list, still per session>
- deny path: the model receives "user denied tool call" as the tool result; no retry without a new prompt

## Resources (read-only data)

- trigger: first `resources/read` for a URI prefix (e.g. `file://`, `db://`)
- surface: <same surface as tools, with a "read" badge>
- shows: verified server name, URI prefix, data class ({{ public_internal_pii }})
- cache scope: per URI prefix, per session
- deny path: resource read returns empty; model is told the read was refused

## Prompts (templates)

- trigger: user picks a server prompt from the host's prompt list
- surface: prompt list entry shows the server label next to the prompt name
- rule r3: prompt body is rendered for the user to read before it is sent; server text is never auto-inserted into the system prompt
- cache scope: none; each selection is an explicit user action
- deny path: user closes the preview; nothing is sent

## Sampling (server asks the host to call the model)

- trigger: `sampling/createMessage` from a server
- surface: {{ modal }}, blocking; shows the full messages the server wants sent and the model it asks for
- rule r1: host approval is mandatory each time; no per-session cache for sampling
- deny path: server receives a JSON-RPC error; the host logs the attempt

## Audit record (rule r6)

```json
{"ts": "<ISO-8601>", "server_id": "<verified-name>", "primitive": "tool|resource|prompt|sampling",
 "tool_name": "<name>", "caller_session": "<session-id>", "arguments_hash": "<sha256>",
 "decision": "allow_once|allow_session|deny", "outcome": "ok|error|denied"}
```

## Review

- cadence: monthly | quarterly
- next_review_at: <YYYY-MM-DD>
- outcome: <filled at next review>
